# ── Written by a script, so formatting them is a loop ────────────────────
#
# `fixtures/exams/*.json` and the assembled packages under `_workspace/` are
# produced by `scripts/assemble-*.py` with `json.dumps(indent=2)`, which always
# expands a short array; Prettier always collapses one. Formatting them once
# rewrites ~320 lines in a single fixture and the next assemble run puts them
# straight back, so `format:check` goes red again for a reason no reader can
# act on. Whoever owns the generator owns the formatting.
fixtures/exams/
_workspace/

# ── Recorded, not authored ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Verbatim provider responses, replayed by the evaluation tests. A recording
# that has been reformatted is no longer the thing that came back off the
# wire, which is the only property that makes it worth keeping.
# → CLAUDE.md, "recorded AI responses, kept per docs/security"
fixtures/ai/

# Tool-owned: `.design-sync` holds a config and generated component previews.
.design-sync/

# ── Binary and owner-supplied source material ────────────────────────────
#
# Prettier reads every path it is not told to skip, and on a 1.3 GB archive it
# does not skip gracefully: `prettier --check .` died with
# `Unable to read file "Đề IELTS/Đề CAM.rar": Invalid string length` — a Node
# string-length ceiling, reached while slurping the archive into memory to
# decide it has no parser. Exit code 2, so the whole formatting gate failed and
# stayed failed, and nobody could tell a real style problem from this.
#
# The directory is the owner's IELTS source material — the same class of
# third-party content as `/exam/`, and gitignored for the same reason.
"Đề IELTS/"

